<article class="env-lemma" id="09HC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09HC">Lemma <span data-tag="09HC">9.12.13</span>.</a> Let $E/k$ be a field extension. Then the elements of $E$ separable over $k$ form a subextension of $E/k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\alpha , \beta \in E$ be separable over $k$. Then $\beta $ is separable over $k(\alpha )$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/09H2" data-tag="09H2">9.12.3</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/09H9" data-tag="09H9">9.12.10</a> (applied with $n = 2$, $\alpha _1 = \alpha $, and $\alpha _2 = \beta $) we see that $k(\alpha , \beta )$ is separable over $k$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>